The Sekan algorithm — a Simpson-rule-based adaptive optimization method
for morphologically-rich low-resource languages — was invented by
Mathew Sekanjako in 2025 as part of the Alkebulan AI research programme.

The ABLT (Alkebulan Bantu-Luganda Tokenizer) architecture — a two-stage
morphologically-aware tokenizer combining a language-specific symbolic
layer with a universal SentencePiece Unigram sub-word model — was
designed by Mathew Sekanjako in 2025 as part of the same programme.

